    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The evidence presents a genuinely balanced situation for AMZN. The near-term tape is bearish \u2014 price is below the 50-day SMA ($177.17) and 10-day EMA, RSI collapsed from 72 to 39, MACD histogram is expanding negative at -1.26, and volume is elevated at 1.59x on the down move, indicating distribution. However, the long-term trend remains intact with price 16.7% above the rising 200-day SMA, and the fortress balance sheet ($84.95B operating cash flow, $201.88B equity) supports the view that this is a pullback within an uptrend rather than a structural breakdown. With no identifiable negative catalyst and the stock trading at ~$174.63, neither adding into a falling knife nor exiting an intact uptrend is justified. The upcoming earnings report is the key binary catalyst that will likely break this balance. I will maintain the current position and set clear triggers: reclaim of the 50-day SMA on above-average volume supports adding, while a break below $171.96 (March 11 swing low) warrants trimming by one-third to one-half.\n\n**Entry Price**: 174.63\n\n**Stop Loss**: 171.96\n\n**Position Sizing**: Neutral-to-moderate weight; do not deploy fresh capital until the 50-day SMA reclaim confirms the setup. If the downside trigger ($171.96) is hit, reduce exposure by roughly one-third to one-half of the current position.\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
